[2.008, "o", "\u001b[1;2H\u001b[1mReverseEngineer(Adrastea) • $\u001b[C6.63 • 25 calls • 16 turns • 12m 51s\r\n\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93m💬 reply #q-ransomware\u001b[36m\u001b[1m ReverseEngineer(Adrastea)\u001b(B\u001b[m                                                                  \u001b[2C                          \r\n\u001b[93m\u001b[1mRefutation evidence from the capability enumeration (#q-capabilities !129–!135):\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93m the file-enumeration loop feeds the\u001b[1m grabber/upload\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93m path, not any\u001b[39m  \r\n\u001b[93mencryption. The generic engine (FUN_140008b30 + grabber_enum_files_pathmatchspec, resolved FindFirstFileA/FindNextFileA/PathMatchSpecA) selects files\r\nby server-supplied masks (csidl/start_path/masks/recursive/max_size/iterations), reads/copies them and\u001b[1m uploads them to the C2\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93m via the\u001b[39m       \r\n\u001b[93mupload_file/filename/data JSON message (FUN_140009814). The only crypto in the binary is (a) RC4 decryption of its own strings (key CgeOvEO7hu), (b)\r\nDPAPI/NSS/ABE\u001b[1m decryption\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93m of browser secrets. No file-encryption loop, no ransom-note string, no extension-rename logic exists in the 276 decrypted\r\nstrings or the plaintext string set (full .rdata/.data coverage per #q-string-decryption !87/!94). The detector's T1486 \"candidate symmetric keys\"\r\nare all accounted for as RC4-encrypted strings (#q-crypto-keys !112). This is a smash-and-grab infostealer (config-gated self-delete after exfil,\r\n#q-persistence !105/!106) —\u001b[1m not ransomware\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[93m. Calibration caveat: the loader tasking can fetch arbitrary follow-on payloads, so \"no ransomware\r\ndelivered later by the operator\" is not claimed.\u001b[39m  \u001b[52C            \u001b[3C               \u001b[7C        \r\n                            \u001b[C                     \u001b[52C            \u001b[3C              \u001b[8C        \r\n\u001b[97m🤖\u001b[36m\u001b[1m ReverseEngineer(Adrastea)\u001b[C\u001b(B\u001b[m                   \u001b[54C            \u001b[3C          \u001b[12C        \r\n\u001b[97m\u001b[1mFinal handoff — capability enumeration for #q-capabilities (Stealc v2, C2 45.93.20.28).\u001b[15C\u001b(B\u001b[m            \u001b[3C          \u001b[12C        \r\n                            \u001b[C               \u001b[58C            \u001b[3C           \u001b[11C        \r\n\u001b[97m\u001b[1mStatus:\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[97m All nine requested components posted as evidence comments under #q-capabilities (!129–!135), plus the full C2 message sequence (!136 under\u001b[39m \r\n\u001b[97m#q-c2-protocol), a ransomware refutation (!137 under #q-ransomware), and the delegated\u001b[1m global→plaintext map of all 276 decrypted-string globals\u001b(B\u001b[m    \r\n\u001b[97m(!115/!117/!118/!120). Question left unsolved for the coordinator, as instructed.\u001b[21C\u001b[39m            \u001b[3C           \u001b[11C        \r\n                            \u001b[C           \u001b[62C            \u001b[3C        \u001b[14C        \r\n\u001b[97m\u001b[1mKey findings (with evidence):\u001b(B\u001b[m           \u001b[62C            \u001b[3C         \u001b[13C        \r\n                            \u001b[C        \u001b[65C            \u001b[3C           \u001b[11C        \r\n\u001b[94m1.\u001b[97m\u001b[1m Config fetch\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[97m FUN_140026214: beacon\u001b[93m {type:\"create\", hwid:<volume-serial GUID>, build}\u001b[97m → config parsed by FUN_140025b64 (opcode\u001b[39m \u001b[10C        \r\n\u001b[93msuccess\u001b[97m/\u001b[93mblocked\u001b[97m→ExitProcess;\u001b[93m access_token\u001b[97m; bools self_delete/take_screenshot/loader/steal_steam/steal_outlook @ +0x40..0x44; arrays\u001b[8C\u001b[39m        \r\n\u001b[97mbrowsers/plugins/files). Task-object parser FUN_140025fa0 = loader-task fields url/csidl/run_as_admin/type. Builder artifact:\u001b[39m     \u001b[9C        \r\n\u001b[93mC:\\builder_v2\\stealc\\json.h\u001b[97m assert path (!129).\u001b[70C\u001b[39m            \u001b[10C        \r\n\u001b[94m2.\u001b[97m\u001b[1m Orchestrator\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[97m FUN_140029f68 flow fully wired (!130): browse\u001b(B\u001b[m"]
[0.000, "o", "\u001b[97mrs type 1/2 → chrome ABE/v10 paths (FUN_14001f100, per #q-embedded-pe), type 3 → Gecko\r\nFUN_1400225ac; files → grabber FUN_140008b30; steal_steam → FUN_140037704; loader flag → FUN_140029900 (early vs post-done); self_delete →\u001b[C\u001b[39m        \r\n\u001b[97m0x14003b870.\u001b[105C\u001b[39m                    \u001b[2C        \r\n\u001b[94m3.\u001b[97m\u001b[1m Loader\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[97m (!131): FUN_140029900 polls\u001b[93m {type:\"loader\"}\u001b[97m, dispatches task types 0/1/2 → FUN_140028978 (.exe+ShellExecuteExA/runas, confirmed) /\u001b[39m       \r\n\u001b[97mFUN_140028e58 / FUN_140029224 (msiexec\u001b[93m /passive\u001b[97m vs powershell IEX strings present).\u001b[34C\u001b[39m          \u001b[12C        \r\n\u001b[94m4.\u001b[97m\u001b[1m Steam theft\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[97m FUN_140037704 decompiled in full (!132): HKCU\u001b[93m Software\\Valve\\Steam\u001b[97m→\u001b[93mSteamPath\u001b[97m→\u001b[93m\\config\\\u001b[97m +\u001b[93m ssfn*,config.vdf,...\u001b[97m masks fed to the generic\r\ngrabber.\u001b[109C\u001b[39m            \u001b[10C        \r\n\u001b[94m5.\u001b[97m\u001b[1m Grabber/wallets\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[97m (!133):\u001b[93m wallets\u001b[97m global's only consumer is grabber_enum_files_pathmatchspec (0x1400084a4) — desktop-wallet theft is entirely\u001b[39m     \r\n\u001b[97mserver-config-driven, no hardcoded wallet list.\u001b[70C\u001b[39m    \u001b[18C        \r\n\u001b[94m6. \u001b[97m\u001b[1mChromium + Firefox theft\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[97m (!134), \u001b[1mscreenshot (JPEG quality 90 → screenshot.jpg upload) + sysinfo profiler\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[97m (!135).\u001b[2C\u001b[39m              \u001b[8C        \u001b[36;118H          \u001b[12C        \r\n\u001b[97m\u001b[1mWhat remains (flagged in-thread; flag_for_review was blocked by context restriction):\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[97m (a) byte-verify whether the screenshot block is gated by\u001b[39m     \r\n\u001b[97mtake_screenshot(+0x41) — decompile shows it unconditional; (b)\u001b[1m no consumer of steal_outlook(+0x44) found\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[97m and no Outlook strings exist — likely\u001b[39m     \r\n\u001b[97mparsed-but-dead in this build, needs confirmation; (c) decompile FUN_140028e58/FUN_140029224 to pin type1↔msi vs type2↔powershell; (d) FUN_14003a430\r\ninternals (multi-monitor?), FUN_1400225ac internals, and\u001b[93m soft\u001b[97m/\u001b[93msoft_path\u001b[97m global consumers.\u001b[28C\u001b[39m       \u001b[15C        \u001b[41;118H                \u001b[6C        \u001b[42;2H\u001b[90mj/k scroll  PgUp/PgDn page\u001b[2CG\u001b[Cbottom\u001b[C click expand  Esc back  q close\u001b(B\u001b[m"]
